Z||000016||Alex4mula||06-09-2000||10:06 AM||||Very nice! Thanks AL for the photos. It fit but like I heard is tight. Look how the pipes start bending down right from the muffler exit. A muffler shop told me that because of that they cannot do it in SS. I think that's BS. Tell your shop to fabricate several SS units and sell it here in the forum. You will get several customers if priced right.||||reg||1
Z||000017||lowCG||06-09-2000||09:16 PM||||All that would be needed to reproduce that system is a piece of plywood with additional pieces of wood to support the un-welded tubes,and a drawing,or outline of each tube before it's welded in,would take all day Saturday,but might be worth it if he could sell maybe five or more.<BR>How much did he say he was going to charge,if you talked about that yet?||||reg||1
Z||000018||AL||06-09-2000||10:04 PM||||ok guys, it's installed, my baby sounds so good, it sounds tough,let me tell you that the muffler is not a tight fit it goes in and out easily, and the way i cut the pipes off it fit very well, i would recomend you buy thi muffer and put it in, all the myths that have been said buy others, are all false. this baby,KICKS ASS also the muffler shop that did it told me it's a good thing i bought this muffler instead of the delta muffler, he said those mufflers don't sound so good like the original flowmaster that i bought, so go ahead spend your money on the other muffler but you won't get the sound that the trans am flowy makes,it sounds so sweet i wish i could put it on for you, but i just don't know how to do it.WATCH OUT RICERS, HERE I COME, AND YOU WILL HEAR ME COMMIN!!!!!!!||||reg||14
